IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `esc-rules`

-- Epidemiological Studies (Confidentiality) Act 1981 (Cth) — the encoder's
-- tests.

§ `Tests`

GIVEN s IS A `Study`, src IS A `Source of information`, act IS A `What I do`, purp IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A `Recipient`
GIVETH A `Study case`
`in` s `having got it` src `I` act `for the study` purp `to` r MEANS
    `Study case` OF s, `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`, src, TRUE, act, purp, r, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`vvs` MEANS `the Vietnam Veterans Study`

-- s 4: telling a journalist.
#ASSERT `it is an offence` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`)
-- for the study: no offence
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` TRUE `to` `someone else`))
-- s 7
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `the only person it concerns`))
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `a person nominated by one of those persons`))
-- s 7 does not cover making a record.
#ASSERT `it is an offence` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `make a record of it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `the only person it concerns`)
-- not a prescribed study
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`in` `another study` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`))
-- s 6: via a s 5 authorisation
#ASSERT `it is an offence` (`in` `a Commonwealth study declared by the regulations` `having got it` `by access to another study's document under a section 5 authorisation` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`)
-- s 5 defence
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`Study case` OF `vvs`, `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`, `by assisting in the study`, TRUE, `give a person assisting another prescribed study access to a document`, FALSE, `someone else`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `it is an offence` (`Study case` OF `vvs`, `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`, `by assisting in the study`, TRUE, `give a person assisting another prescribed study access to a document`, FALSE, `someone else`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- s 3(2): a subject of the study is not bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`Study case` OF `vvs`, `I am only a subject or gave information about a subject`, `by assisting in the study`, TRUE, `divulge or communicate it`, FALSE, `someone else`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
-- s 11
#ASSERT NOT (`it is an offence` (`Study case` OF `vvs`, `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`, `by assisting in the study`, TRUE, `divulge or communicate it`, FALSE, `someone else`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE))
-- s 8
#ASSERT `may I be required to give it to a court` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `may I be required to give it to a court` (`in` `another study` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10
#ASSERT `must I take the oath` (`Study case` OF `vvs`, `I conduct, supervise or assist in it`, `otherwise`, FALSE, `make a record of it`, FALSE, `someone else`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT (`the study position for` (`in` `vvs` `having got it` `by assisting in the study` `I` `divulge or communicate it` `for the study` FALSE `to` `someone else`))'s `maximum penalty units` EQUALS 10
